      {
        "id": "2013624161894060289",
        "type": "tweet",
        "url": "https://x.com/QUBelfast/status/2013624161894060289",
        "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/QUBelfast/status/2013624161894060289",
        "text": "We have started construction on the expanded Momentum One Zero innovation centre, our business-led facility focused on #cybersecurity, #ArtificialIntelligence and #wireless technologies.\n\nDelivered as part of the £70 million Belfast Region City Deal investment, @QUBMomentum10 will act as a focal point for industry-led digital innovation, supporting collaboration across sectors including health, agri-food, financial services, sustainability, and advanced manufacturing.\n\nWe were joined on site by key representatives from government, civic, academic, and industry to cut the sod at Belfast’s Titanic Quarter.\n\n“Momentum One Zero is a clear example of how Queen’s is turning research excellence into economic impact. This expansion reflects the scale of ambition we have for digital innovation in #NorthernIreland — supporting high-value jobs, strengthening our skills base, and ensuring that businesses here can compete and lead on a global stage.” (Professor Sir Ian Greer, @QUBVChancellor)\n\nFind out more here ➡️ https://t.co/jtDJeYuead\n\n#LoveQUB | #BRCityDeal | #CityDeal | @QUBCityDeal | @belfastcc | @Economy_NI",
